# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages
#
# index.html is the one file that cannot be cache-busted by URL — it IS the URL.
# So it must be revalidated on every load. js/ and css/ carry a ?v= query that
# changes with the app version, but we revalidate them too so that editing a
# file without bumping the version can't strand anyone on stale code.
#
# "no-cache" does NOT mean "don't cache" — it means "check with me first".
# The browser still keeps the file and the server answers 304 when unchanged,
# so this costs almost nothing.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
